WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.372
Laurie walked into Grandpa's study wearing a necklace and a long dress pinned at the shoulders.

2
00:00:08.373 --> 00:00:10.688
Her hair was gathered into a net.

3
00:00:10.689 --> 00:00:14.765
"How do I look, Grandpa? Can you guess what I am for Halloween?"

4
00:00:14.766 --> 00:00:19.666
"A woman from ancient Greece of course!" Grandpa said, smiling.

5
00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:23.870
"And which city-state, may I ask, are you from?"

6
00:00:23.871 --> 00:00:27.149
Laurie frowned. "I hadn't really thought about it.

7
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:34.253
Sparta? Athens?" she answered, naming the only two old Greek cities she knew.

8
00:00:34.254 --> 00:00:41.135
"Those are two very different cities. They were also enemies for many years.

9
00:00:41.136 --> 00:00:46.819
Maybe I should tell you about them so you can decide which one you'd rather live in.

10
00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:52.026
The Spartans were known for being serious, disciplined warriors.

11
00:00:52.027 --> 00:00:57.103
Every man joined the army and spent most of his life in the military.

12
00:00:57.104 --> 00:01:04.757
Training began at age seven, when boys were taken from their families and sent to live in military camps.

13
00:01:04.758 --> 00:01:12.759
They practiced sports for hours each day because having a weak body was considered dishonorable among Spartans.

14
00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:17.456
They were taught to live with only the barest necessities.

15
00:01:17.457 --> 00:01:26.314
Sometimes they were even starved on purpose so they would learn to fearlessly steal or kill their own food for survival.

16
00:01:26.315 --> 00:01:34.619
They were also served a black soup made of pork stewed in pigs' blood, vinegar, and salt to make them strong.

17
00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:41.001
Besides undergoing physical training, they had to learn how to become brave warriors.

18
00:01:41.002 --> 00:01:47.591
A good Spartan warrior could never cry out in pain or surrender easily.

19
00:01:47.592 --> 00:01:52.268
Even the Spartan women were expected to be strong and fearless.

20
00:01:52.269 --> 00:02:03.234
Unlike women in most other Greek cities, women of Sparta spent lots of time outdoors, exercising: they ran, did gymnastics, and danced.

21
00:02:03.235 --> 00:02:13.087
Part of a woman's duty was to provide her husband with a physically fit—preferably male—child who would become a strong warrior.

22
00:02:13.088 --> 00:02:20.349
In order to give birth to a healthy child, it was thought the mother must be fit and healthy too.

23
00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:25.958
Girls also received good educations and were allowed to own property as adults!

24
00:02:25.959 --> 00:02:31.514
This really shocked Greeks from other cities, where women weren't allowed such things.

25
00:02:31.515 --> 00:02:37.994
Spartan men and women were able to devote their lives to building a powerful Spartan military

26
00:02:37.995 --> 00:02:42.498
because all their farming and other labor was done by slaves.

27
00:02:42.499 --> 00:02:47.456
In fact, most of Sparta's economy ran on slave labor.

28
00:02:47.457 --> 00:02:52.155
But just because they had slaves doesn't mean Spartans were extravagant.

29
00:02:52.156 --> 00:02:55.646
They were expected to scorn wealth and luxury.

30
00:02:55.647 --> 00:03:01.943
They didn't have parties and, besides religious rites, had very few celebrations.

31
00:03:01.944 --> 00:03:05.189
They didn't wear jewelry or make much art.

32
00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:11.771
Today the word 'spartan' can describe someone who is courageous and self-disciplined,

33
00:03:11.772 --> 00:03:17.107
but also something that is extremely simple and not at all luxurious.

34
00:03:17.108 --> 00:03:21.511
What do you say, Laurie, could you be a Spartan?"

35
00:03:21.512 --> 00:03:27.887
"Hmm . . . I could play sports, learn stuff, and eventually own my own house.

36
00:03:27.888 --> 00:03:34.324
That doesn't sound so bad, but I want to hear about Athens before I decide," Laurie said.

37
00:03:34.325 --> 00:03:40.561
"You got it. Athenians enjoyed a lifestyle very different from the Spartans.

38
00:03:40.562 --> 00:03:47.291
Women's main duties were to raise children, take care of the household, and weave wool.

39
00:03:47.292 --> 00:03:53.432
If you were an Athenian, you probably would have made that beautiful dress of yours at home.

40
00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:59.110
Now taking care of the household could mean different things depending on how rich you were.

41
00:03:59.111 --> 00:04:06.346
If you were well-off, you probably had many slaves who would clean, watch the children, and bake bread.

42
00:04:06.347 --> 00:04:11.082
If you weren't, well, you might be doing all that work yourself.

43
00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:18.028
Although boys began school around age seven, Athenian girls didn't get to go to school.

44
00:04:18.029 --> 00:04:24.783
Around age 13 or so, they got married and began their lives as wives and mothers.

45
00:04:24.784 --> 00:04:28.284
But Athens was a truly incredible city.

46
00:04:28.285 --> 00:04:37.621
It is often called the birthplace of democracy because it was the first city to test out democracy, or government run by citizens.

47
00:04:37.622 --> 00:04:46.941
Athenians held city meetings at which all citizens—meaning Greek men who were born in the city—could share their opinions.

48
00:04:46.942 --> 00:04:55.121
Then citizens were allowed to vote. Sometimes they decided big issues, such as whether the city should go to war.

49
00:04:55.122 --> 00:05:01.043
Their style of government developed into the democracy we know today.

50
00:05:01.044 --> 00:05:10.402
Athens was also home to the famous Acropolis, an immense complex of temples, theaters, and other impressive buildings.

51
00:05:10.403 --> 00:05:15.775
The temples were dedicated to the worship of the Greeks' many gods and goddesses,

52
00:05:15.776 --> 00:05:20.613
whom the Athenians respected, feared, and often celebrated.

53
00:05:20.614 --> 00:05:25.052
Athenians were not spartan like the Spartans.

54
00:05:25.053 --> 00:05:32.335
They enjoyed sculpture, music, theater, poetry, and philosophy.

55
00:05:32.336 --> 00:05:36.543
Maybe you've heard of the great thinkers Socrates and Aristotle?

56
00:05:36.544 --> 00:05:46.763
They were both from Athens. Athenian citizens were deep thinkers, but they also liked wine, feasts, and celebrations!

57
00:05:46.764 --> 00:05:56.394
Grooming was also an important part of life; both men and women took hot baths and rubbed themselves with olive oil.

58
00:05:56.395 --> 00:06:00.049
Women owned lots of makeup and perfume.

59
00:06:00.050 --> 00:06:07.327
Athenians wore beautiful gold jewelry, a lot of which can be seen in museums today.

60
00:06:07.328 --> 00:06:16.806
Sparta and Athens had very different ideas about how people should live and govern themselves, but each grew to be a strong city.

61
00:06:16.807 --> 00:06:28.268
Eventually they clashed. Both wanted to rule the other Greek city-states, and in 431 BC, they fought in the Peloponnesian War.

62
00:06:28.269 --> 00:06:36.778
After nearly thirty years of battle, the Spartans were victorious and the good times in Athens ended.

63
00:06:36.779 --> 00:06:40.021
So what do you think, my little Grecian?

64
00:06:40.022 --> 00:06:47.169
Which ancient city would you like to live in—Sparta or Athens?" Grandpa asked.

65
00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:55.924
Laurie considered her options. "Being a Spartan would mean I'd live a simple—and maybe harsh—life, but get to run around a lot.

66
00:06:55.925 --> 00:07:04.473
Being an Athenian would mean I'd witness the birth and development of democracy, but I wouldn't get to participate because I'm a girl.

67
00:07:04.474 --> 00:07:14.013
Sparta it is!" Laurie cried, snatching off her necklace and raising a fist in the air. She marched out of the study.

68
00:07:14.014 --> 00:07:17.812
"Lace up your sneakers, Mom," she called.

69
00:07:17.813 --> 00:07:26.603
"We're jogging to the Halloween parade—in true Spartan style!"

